{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MX-012","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D10","page":1,"quote":"22"}],"comment":"Dimension D10 defines the width of the keyway slot (F2), which is a functional mating feature for torque transmission, yet it carries no tolerance and falls back on the general ±0.2 mm. A keyway width requires a specific fit tolerance to ensure proper engagement with the key; the designer should add an appropriate tolerance class or limit dimensions to D10."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Add a specific fit tolerance (e.g., H9 or P9) or explicit limit dimensions to D10 for the keyway width."}]}
